**WAKING FROM INNOCENT DREAMS** is {{{genre}}} with elements of magical realism. A cross between HADES, ARGENTINA and THE VOLCANO DAUGHTERS, it will also appeal to readers who liked A BEAST SLINKS TOWARDS BEIJING. This coming-of-age story, complete at 110,000 words, spans twenty years and follows a boy who survived and a ghost who remembers.

Growing up, Nelson’s family loved him but looked nothing like him. He longs to meet the one person he believes will make him whole, while trying to ignore the ghost that won't leave him alone. Then a positive DNA test reveals him to be Roberto, the son of Salvadoran revolutionaries who, as an infant, was *desaparecido* during a violent government raid. At a miraculous reunion, Nelson meets a family ready to welcome him home, except for the one person who was disappeared alongside him: his mother.

After he travels to Central America, his past and present blend, thunderstorms drown out discontent, and living rooms expand to fit the entire neighborhood. Over the years, as he discovers a life taken from him, he struggles to balance the demands of his two lives, leaving him feeling *ni de aquí ni de allá*. Just as Nelson comes to terms with the cost of his disappearance, a betrayal forces him to make an impossible choice: protect the family he has dreamed of since childhood, or accept the truth his ghost and siblings have been pushing him toward.

Since the 1950s, governments throughout Latin America have abducted more than 100,000 people as a strategy of intimidation and control. Only a small handful, almost all children, reunite with their families. Of those, a tiny fraction get a second chance to grow up with the family they were taken from.

As one of El Salvador’s Disappeared Children, I am part of that tiny fraction who received a second chance. My novel may be the first English-language novel about forced disappearances written by someone who was taken by the state and later reunited with their family. My writing has appeared in _NACLA Report on the Americas_, and my story has been featured in the BBC World Service, _Los Angeles Times_, _Christian Science Monitor_, and _Huffington Post_. I am also completing a documentary film, IDENTIFYING NELSON/BUSCANDO A ROBERTO, which offers natural co-marketing opportunities for the book.

